      "mentions": 23,
      "title": {
        "en": "Supportive clinicians and helpful veterinary assistants"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "The overwhelming majority of pet owners praise Dr Herrera, Dr Klinger, and the nursing team for their empathy, clinical competence, and calming presence. Families report decades of consistent care and appreciate that clinicians take time to explain treatment options without pressurising owners into unnecessary tests. A small number of reviewers, however, voiced frustration over interactions with management or relief personnel."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "mentions": 17,
      "title": {
        "en": "Attentive care for cats and dogs"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients frequently commend the practice for handling anxious, fragile, or aggressive companion animals with patience and kindness. Cat owners highlight the clinic's gentle approach when assessing older feline patients or administering routine vaccines, while dog owners note compassionate support during end-of-life care and post-surgical recuperation. Pets are consistently treated with genuine affection and respect."
      }
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "mentions": 6,
      "title": {
        "en": "Follow-up calls alongside prescription disputes"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Feedback regarding customer communication presents a varied picture. Satisfied clients appreciate proactive follow-up telephone calls the day after appointments and prompt answers to health questions. Conversely, critical reviewers experienced friction regarding external medication approvals, rigid electronic prescription policies, and perceived discourtesy from front desk staff during administrative inquiries."
      }
    }
  ],
